<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eric XIV of Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1533">1533</a>–<a href="/years/1577">1577</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eric XIV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-i-of-sweden">Gustav Vasa</a>, was king from 1560 to 1568. In 1561 Reval and the knighthoods of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a> submitted to him, beginning Swedish rule there and drawing Sweden into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livonian-war">Livonian War</a>. In 1563 he crushed the independent Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> of his half-brother John. Mental illness and political murders weakened him, and John deposed him in 1568; he died a prisoner.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eric-xiv-of-sweden.jpg" alt="Eric XIV of Sweden" width="320" height="471" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Domenicus Verwilt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erik_XIV_king_of_Sweden_1533-1577_(Domenicus_Verwilt)_-_Nationalmuseum_-_21667.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
